From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: map submitqueue priorities onto HIGH..LOW in order

msm_gpu_convert_priority() still inverts the per-ring priority from before
drm_sched reversed its priority enum (lower values are higher priority
since then, with KERNEL at 0). With NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES = 3, userspace
priority 0 (the highest) became DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_NORMAL and userspace
priority 2 (the lowest) became DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_KERNEL.

On a single-ring Adreno 650 Turnip maps Vulkan's REALTIME to 0 and MEDIUM
(the default) to 2. gamescope asks for REALTIME when it has CAP_SYS_NICE,
so the compositor's queue ran at NORMAL while every game's default queue
ran at KERNEL and Mesa's OpenGL contexts at HIGH: whenever a game kept the
GPU busy, the compositor waited behind it.

Map 0..2 onto HIGH..LOW in order and index the entity array from HIGH.
The scheduler of each ring has DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_COUNT run queues, so
HIGH, NORMAL and LOW are all valid.

Based on the same fix in SteamOS-ARM-Handhelds by hashtagbasit
(external-and-mods/kernel-sm8550/patches/0012), which reports that
ArmadaOS found the same problem; this version has no VM_BIND queues to
keep at KERNEL, as 6.16 has none.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
@@ -447,8 +447,8 @@
  * is mapped to ring nr and scheduler priority as such:
  *
  *   ring_nr    = userspace_prio / NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES
- *   sched_prio = NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES -
- *                (userspace_prio % NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) - 1
+ *   sched_prio = DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH +
+ *                (userspace_prio % NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES)
  *
  * This allows generations without preemption (nr_rings==1) to have some
  * amount of prioritization, and provides more priority levels for gens
@@ -461,10 +461,15 @@
 
 	rn = div_u64_rem(prio, NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES, &sp);
 
-	/* invert sched priority to map to higher-numeric-is-higher-
-	 * priority convention
+	/*
+	 * Lower userspace values are higher priority, and since drm_sched
+	 * reversed its enum so are lower drm_sched_priority values: map 0..2
+	 * onto HIGH..LOW in order. The old inversion put each ring's highest
+	 * userspace priority at NORMAL and its lowest at KERNEL, so a game's
+	 * default queue outranked a compositor that asked for a high
+	 * priority (gamescope).
 	 */
-	sp = NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES - sp - 1;
+	sp += DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH;
 
 	if (rn >= gpu->nr_rings)
 		return -EINVAL;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_submitqueue.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_submitqueue.c
@@ -123,7 +123,8 @@
 		 unsigned ring_nr, enum drm_sched_priority sched_prio)
 {
 	static DEFINE_MUTEX(entity_lock);
-	unsigned idx = (ring_nr * NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) + sched_prio;
+	unsigned idx = (ring_nr * NR_SCHED_PRIORITIES) +
+		       (sched_prio - DRM_SCHED_PRIORITY_HIGH);
 
 	/* We should have already validated that the requested priority is
 	 * valid by the time we get here.
